/**
 * The reviewed Spanish, in a module with no React in it.
 *
 * These lived in `app/components/site-language.tsx`, which is `"use client"`.
 * Anything server-side that imported them — the crawler-facing translation in
 * `spanish-html.ts`, and any Worker route built on it — dragged React into the
 * Cloudflare Worker bundle with them. A plain module has no such edge.
 *
 * `site-language.tsx` imports and re-exports both, so every existing importer
 * is unchanged and the browser still reads exactly these strings.
 *
 * **`scripts/check-spanish-coverage.mjs` parses this file.** It reads the
 * entries below with a line-anchored regex to prove every string on a
 * Spanish-ready page is translated, and fails the build when one is not. Keep
 * the two-space indentation, and if these ever move again, move the guard in
 * the same change — split them and the build quietly stops checking.
 */

